mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|mb|1C|mb|P|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East has an interesting problem normally with 5-5 you bid your highest suit first and then your lower suit because that allows partner to correct to your higher suit without going up a level. However, if East were not a passed hand and and bids 1@S she is not strong enough to bid 2@H if partner rebids 2@C. Regardless, 1@S is the perfect bid.|
PG| ***** 2 ***** |


mb|1S|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|4S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|West is correct to jump to game, though, 4@H is a slightly better bid. 4@H is a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=splinters,Splinter^*N|CP||FP||at|. On this auction it shows 20 points, 4 spades, and a singleton heart. But we play the hand 4@S.|

