%%%% Hand 4
https://tinyurl.com/29jz8x4u
qx|A4|st||rh||ah|Board 4 IMPs   -   June 12, 2024|pn|hondo717,marikaSz,aspiring,coxenrider|
md|2SQJT87HKQJ9DAKCT5,S952HAT762DQT63C3,S64H853DJ8752C762,SAK3H4D94CAKQJ984|sv|b|
mb|P|mb|P|mb|1C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|1@C is fine and reasonable. However, technically East has a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=open2c,2C Openers^*N|cp||fp||at| opener. You can open 2@C if you have a hand with 4 quick tricks and can count 9 winners. East does have 4 quick tricks and has 7 clubs and 2 spades for 9 tricks.|
PG| ***** 60 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Having said that, when you open 2@C with a long minor, that is what I call ^*BSelf Preempting.^*n What I mean by that is if you open 2@C and partner responds 2@D you have to bid 3@C. So you are already at the 3 level before you make a natural bid.|
PG| ***** 61 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Therefore, on any hand where you have a long minor and a 2@C opener, like the East hand, opening at the one level is often better.|
PG| ***** 62 ***** |


MB|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|With both majors I could double as many players would. On the other hand, when I am 5-4 in the majors and have a choice between doubling and overcalling my 5-card suit I tend to bid my 5-card suit. Otherwise you will never get across that you have a 5-card major.|
PG| ***** 63 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|That is not really a big issue unless partner is short in your 5-card suit and has 4-card support for your 4-card suit. On this hand, however, because I have 2 quality suit majors (3 honors each) I am going to double.|
PG| ***** 64 ***** |


mb|D|mb|1H|mb|P|MB|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East should now bid 3N after a good bid by West. Yes, opponents might be running 5 diamonds and beat the contract. But that is highly unlikely because I have to lead a diamond and to have 5 diamonds in one hand, which is somewhat unlikely given I made a takeout double.|
PG| ***** 65 ***** |


mb|3N|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 66 ***** |


